  "claims": [
    "QuantitativeReduction retains the actual reduction, typed finite compiler and its code/execution/resource/realization witnesses without assuming that its loss preserves negligible functions. Explicit promotion requires that additional property; ofCertified followed by promotion recovers the original CertifiedReduction.",
    "QuantitativeComparison compares instance families, dependent adversary/code/resource/execution packets, emitted code and actual loss functions. Its composition/groupoid-of-comparisons operations never reverse computational reduction arrows.",
    "QuantitativeReduction.observe changes an observation of one unchanged execution under a separately supplied advantage inequality. observe_comp compares staged and direct observation changes only under an explicit equality of their composed loss functions.",
    "GameProofQuantitative interprets the existing directed condition-bearing Plan/Cell presentation in quantitative reductions, with finite bound transport and repair of comparisons including internal conditions; it supplies no unconditional asymptotic security theorem.",
    "For the same fixed adaptive 8-message/256-tag MAC attack, caller_contract is instantiated from the original universal native caller correctness theorems. It records the same 251-instruction code, a 343-transition horizon, stopping for every key and exactly four actual calls including the repeated query.",
    "native_full_law connects that same continuing native caller to every preparation-order fullLaw, retaining the original success bit, oracle state and all typed query/response pairs. stage_probability_realized ties the observed security advantage to that actual native probability.",
    "Concrete schedule and elimination reductions preserve emitted code and resource data. The original local preparation/elimination diagram is checked on the complete quantitative packets and loss functions; generated comparisons extend it to arbitrary terminal proof plans in the original serial presentation.",
    "For every such terminal plan, emitted_code/resources/extracted_execution/extracted_full_observation/loss/arbitrary_bound retain the original code, 343-transition caller contract, four calls, full state and trace and the exact epsilon+1/256 advantage transformer. The existing finite security bound is reused, not improved.",
    "extracted_process identifies the entire timed caller transition law at every horizon, oracle and frame because the emitted code is identical. Sanitization is separately proved as an analysis readout; the original unsanitized native observation is retained independently.",
    "statisticalLoss_not_negligible formally refutes negligible-function preservation for the particular fixed additive 1/256 loss; it does not refute all alternative bounds or all possible reductions.",
    "Serial is indexed by actual MixedCircuit MAC circuits. Its plan translation preserves required-condition sets exactly, interprets the real boxes and sequence, compares the actual before/after root and repairs it under the actual root support. serial_code proves code preservation by ordinary structural induction without a higher-cell input."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The concrete adversary is the original fixed adaptive MAC attack with all local coin/response cases, represented by a Unit adversary goal. This is not a theorem for arbitrary attackers, security-dependent tag lengths, or a new cryptographic security bound.",
    "The 343 transitions count caller computation and packet transfer. Typed oracle evaluation and initial key-function generation remain external capabilities. The existing 2091-transition native compact backend and its complete physical-state refinement are not yet instantiated in these quantitative objects.",
    "Sanitization changes the declared analysis observation, not the physical program output or its cost. Raw state, trace and original success bit remain available through the independent raw native law.",
    "This concrete semantics maps game-transformation boxes/circuit sequences to reductions and box rewrites to comparisons. It is not a full instantiation of the previous MixedCircuit.Computational.Model that maps rewrite paths themselves to reductions.",
    "The Serial fragment contains atomic identity wiring, actual MAC boxes and sequence. It does not interpret tensor/copy/discard or prove the remaining pure/mixed critical-overlap coverage, finite complete higher basis, all cryptographic/fusion contracts, or unrestricted convergence.",
    "The observation comparison principle and finite quantitative/asymptotic distinction are not asserted novel. Fair ordinary/shared-proof byte/time comparison and theorem-level priority reduction remain undone.",
    "The concrete serial proof edits compile to the identity. serial_code already gives ordinary-induction evidence for code preservation. In accordance with the earlier case-selection criterion this case is retained as an execution-contract validation example, not adopted as the publication centerpiece demonstrating a higher-dimensional advantage. A code-changing reduction/case and fair proof-construction comparison are still needed."
  ],
  "concrete_contract": {
    "caller_instructions": 251,
    "caller_transition_horizon": 343,
    "actual_calls": 4,
    "message_count": 8,
    "tag_count": 256,
    "loss": "epsilon + 1/256",
    "resource_data": "Nat horizon, required to equal 343",
    "oracle_model": "Original typed coordinate oracle via original packet adapter; its internal evaluation is an external capability.",
    "initial_state": "Fully prepared finite-coordinate state (univ, key), with key drawn uniformly in the experiment ensemble; no machine cost for initial key generation is inferred.",
    "retained_observations": [
      "original verification bit",
      "entire oracle state including the key function",
      "entire typed request/response trace",
      "entire timed caller process through emitted-code equality"
    ],
    "publication_case_status": "execution-contract validation; not a distinguishing-advantage centerpiece"
  },
  "novelty": {
    "status": "unconfirmed",
    "finding": "Concrete MAC serial proof boxes and their local comparison now carry the real caller execution/finite-loss contracts. The identity code behavior is also proved by ordinary induction and therefore does not establish a need for higher cells or an advantage over shared ordinary proofs.",
    "next_evidence": "Connect shared-state tensor/copy/discard and all mixed critical overlaps to actual execution contracts, integrate the complete compact native backend refinement, select a code-changing reduction case and compare proof/update costs against ordinary shared proofs with identical information, then complete primary-theorem reductions."
  },
